    "conclusion": "No single factor explains best_iteration == 1; it needs all three together. It occurs only in the cell with the computed scale_pos_weight (about 97), binary_logloss early stopping and patience 50. Removing any one factor removes it: patience 200 on the same cell runs to 400 iterations, average_precision stopping with the same weight runs to 209, and scale_pos_weight 1.0 never stops at 1 under either metric. The heavy positive weight inflates early predicted probabilities, so unweighted validation log loss first worsens while ranking is still improving, and a 50-round patience stops training before it recovers. The one-tree model (ROC-AUC 0.762) was an early-stopping artifact, not a property of the data. Without the weight the model is also better ranked (ROC-AUC 0.944 to 0.956 against 0.880 to 0.889 with it), and every cell beats the single-feature baseline (0.714). The test split has only 58 buyers (0.90 percent), so differences between cells carry wide uncertainty. Re-run in v1.3 on the schema v2 feature SQL; the pattern is unchanged."
